### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a function that can efficiently determine the number of lines of code in a given C# source file. The function should take a string representing the source code as input and return the total number of lines of code, excluding empty lines and lines containing only comments.

For the purpose of this problem, a line of code is defined as any non-empty line that does not solely consist of comments. Comments are considered to be any text following a double forward slash (`//`) until the end of the line.

Your task is to implement the `CountLinesOfCode` function, which takes a string `sourceCode` as input and returns the total number of lines of code in the source file.

Function signature: 
```csharp
public static int CountLinesOfCode(string sourceCode)
```

Example:
```csharp
string sourceCode = @"
using System;

// This is a simple C# program
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Display a message
        Console.WriteLine(""Hello, World!"");
    }
}
";
int linesOfCode = CountLinesOfCode(sourceCode); // Output: 7
```

### Solution:
```csharp
public static int CountLinesOfCode(string sourceCode)
{
    int lines = 0;
    bool inBlockComment = false;

    foreach (string line in sourceCode.Split('\n'))
    {
        string trimmedLine = line.Trim();

        if (trimmedLine.StartsWith("//") || inBlockComment)
        {
            if (trimmedLine.Contains("*/"))
            {
                inBlockComment = false;
            }
            continue;
        }

        if (trimmedLine.StartsWith("/*"))
        {
            inBlockComment = true;
            if (trimmedLine.Contains("*/"))
            {
                inBlockComment = false;
            }
            continue;
        }

        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(trimmedLine))
        {
            lines++;
        }
    }

    return lines;
}
```

