Your task is to complete the implementation of the `Category` class by adding methods to manipulate the tree structure. Specifically, you need to implement the following methods:
1. `addChild(child: Category): void`: This method should add the specified `child` category to the current category's children.
2. `removeChild(child: Category): void`: This method should remove the specified `child` category from the current category's children.
3. `getDescendants(): Category[]`: This method should return an array of all descendant categories of the current category.

You should ensure that the tree structure is maintained correctly when adding or removing children, and when retrieving descendants.

Complete the implementation of the `Category` class to fulfill the requirements.

```typescript
class Category {
  @TreeParent()
  parent?: Category | null;
  children: Category[];

  constructor() {
    this.children = [];
  }

  addChild(child: Category): void {
    this.children.push(child);
    child.parent = this;
  }

  removeChild(child: Category): void {
    const index = this.children.indexOf(child);
    if (index !== -1) {
      this.children.splice(index, 1);
      child.parent = null;
    }
  }

  getDescendants(): Category[] {
    let descendants: Category[] = [];
    for (const child of this.children) {
      descendants.push(child);
      descendants = descendants.concat(child.getDescendants());
    }
    return descendants;
  }
}
```

