### Problem:
You are given a linked list with a cycle. Your task is to implement a function to determine the starting node of the cycle.

You need to write a function `detectCycle` that takes in the head of the linked list and returns the starting node of the cycle if a cycle exists, or `null` if there is no cycle.

The input linked list is represented as follows:
```javascript
class ListNode {
  constructor(val) {
    this.val = val;
    this.next = null;
  }
}
```

The function signature is:
```javascript
/**
 * @param {ListNode} head - The head of the linked list
 * @return {ListNode} - The starting node of the cycle, or null if no cycle exists
 */
function detectCycle(head) {
  // Your code here
}
```

For example, given the following linked list:
```
1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6
          ^           |
          |           v
          9 <- 8 <- 7
```
The function should return the node with value 4, as it is the starting node of the cycle.

### Solution:
```javascript
function detectCycle(head) {
  let slow = head;
  let fast = head;

  while (fast !== null && fast.next !== null) {
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next.next;

    if (slow === fast) {
      let start = head;
      while (start !== slow) {
        start = start.next;
        slow = slow.next;
      }
      return start;
    }
  }

  return null;
}
```

