You need to implement the `processAnnotations` method to iterate through the annotated classes and generate a map with the annotated class names and their corresponding annotations.

For example, given the following annotated classes:
```java
@MyAnnotation("ClassA")
public class ClassA {
    // Class implementation
}

@MyAnnotation("ClassB")
public class ClassB {
    // Class implementation
}

public class ClassC {
    // Class implementation
}
```

The `CustomAnnotationProcessor` should generate a map as follows:
```
{
    "ClassA": ["@MyAnnotation(\"ClassA\")"],
    "ClassB": ["@MyAnnotation(\"ClassB\")"]
}
```

### Solution:
```java
import javax.annotation.processing.AbstractProcessor;
import javax.annotation.processing.RoundEnvironment;
import javax.annotation.processing.SupportedAnnotationTypes;
import javax.annotation.processing.SupportedSourceVersion;
import javax.lang.model.SourceVersion;
import javax.lang.model.element.Element;
import javax.lang.model.element.TypeElement;
import javax.tools.Diagnostic;
import java.util.*;

@SupportedAnnotationTypes("com.example.MyAnnotation")
@SupportedSourceVersion(SourceVersion.RELEASE_8)
public class CustomAnnotationProcessor extends AbstractProcessor {

    @Override
    public boolean process(Set<? extends TypeElement> annotations, RoundEnvironment roundEnv) {
        Map<String, List<String>> annotatedClasses = new HashMap<>();
        for (Element element : roundEnv.getElementsAnnotatedWith(MyAnnotation.class)) {
            if (element instanceof TypeElement) {
                TypeElement typeElement = (TypeElement) element;
                String className = typeElement.getQualifiedName().toString();
                List<String> classAnnotations = new ArrayList<>();
                for (javax.lang.model.element.AnnotationMirror annotationMirror : typeElement.getAnnotationMirrors()) {
                    classAnnotations.add(annotationMirror.toString());
                }
                annotatedClasses.put(className, classAnnotations);
            }
        }
        generateReport(annotatedClasses);
        return true;
    }

    private void generateReport(Map<String, List<String>> annotatedClasses) {
        for (Map.Entry<String, List<String>> entry : annotatedClasses.entrySet()) {
            processingEnv.getMessager().printMessage(Diagnostic.Kind.NOTE, "Annotated Class: " + entry.getKey());
            for (String annotation : entry.getValue()) {
                processingEnv.getMessager().printMessage(Diagnostic.Kind.NOTE, "Annotation: " + annotation);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `CustomAnnotationProcessor` class extends `AbstractProcessor` and overrides the `process` method to process the annotations on classes. It iterates through the annotated elements, extracts the class names and their annotations, and generates a report using the `generateReport` method. The `SupportedAnnotationTypes` and `SupportedSourceVersion` annotations specify the supported annotation types and source version, respectively.

