### Problem:
You are tasked with simulating a distributed key-value store system using Akka actors in Java. The system consists of multiple clients and a checker actor responsible for verifying the correctness of the key-value store. Each client actor is responsible for storing a subset of keys and their corresponding values, and the checker actor ensures that all clients have the correct data.

The code snippet provided initializes the checker actor and sends a start message to the clients to begin the simulation. The `Checker` actor is responsible for coordinating the verification process, and the `Message.WelcomeMsg` contains the maximum key value (`MAX_KEY`) and a list of coordinator actors (`coordinators`). The `startClients` message is sent to each client actor to initiate the key-value storage process.

Your task is to implement the client actor and the checker actor, ensuring that the clients store the correct key-value pairs and the checker actor verifies the correctness of the distributed key-value store.

### Solution:
```java
import akka.actor.AbstractActor;
import akka.actor.ActorRef;
import akka.actor.ActorSystem;
import akka.actor.Props;

import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

// Define the message types
class Message {
    static class WelcomeMsg {
        int maxKey;
        ActorRef[] coordinators;

        WelcomeMsg(int maxKey, ActorRef[] coordinators) {
            this.maxKey = maxKey;
            this.coordinators = coordinators;
        }
    }

    static class KeyValue {
        int key;
        String value;

        KeyValue(int key, String value) {
            this.key = key;
            this.value = value;
        }
    }

    static class VerifyData {
        Map<Integer, String> data;

        VerifyData(Map<Integer, String> data) {
            this.data = data;
        }
    }
}

// Client actor responsible for storing key-value pairs
class Client extends AbstractActor {
    private Map<Integer, String> keyValueStore = new HashMap<>();
    private int maxKey;
    private ActorRef[] coordinators;

    @Override
    public Receive createReceive() {
        return receiveBuilder()
                .match(Message.WelcomeMsg.class, welcomeMsg -> {
                    this.maxKey = welcomeMsg.maxKey;
                    this.coordinators = welcomeMsg.coordinators;
                })
                .match(Message.KeyValue.class, keyValue -> {
                    if (keyValue.key <= maxKey) {
                        keyValueStore.put(keyValue.key, keyValue.value);
                    }
                })
                .build();
    }
}

// Checker actor responsible for verifying the correctness of the key-value store
class Checker extends AbstractActor {
    private Map<ActorRef, Map<Integer, String>> clientData = new HashMap<>();
    private int maxKey;

    @Override
    public Receive createReceive() {
        return receiveBuilder()
                .match(Message.WelcomeMsg.class, welcomeMsg -> {
                    this.maxKey = welcomeMsg.maxKey;
                    for (ActorRef coordinator : welcomeMsg.coordinators) {
                        clientData.put(coordinator, new HashMap<>());
                    }
                })
                .match(Message.KeyValue.class, keyValue -> {
                    if (keyValue.key <= maxKey) {
                        clientData.get(getSender()).put(keyValue.key, keyValue.value);
                    }
                })
                .match(VerifyData.class, verifyData -> {
                    boolean allDataCorrect = clientData.values().stream()
                            .allMatch(data -> data.equals(verifyData.data));
                    if (allDataCorrect) {
                        System.out.println("All client data is correct");
                    } else {
                        System.out.println("Some client data is incorrect");
                    }
                })
                .build();
    }
}

public class DistributedKeyValueStoreSimulation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ActorSystem system = ActorSystem.create("DistributedKeyValueStoreSystem");

        // Create checker actor
        ActorRef checker = system.actorOf(Props.create(Checker.class), "checker");

        // Create client actors
        ActorRef[] clients = new ActorRef[5];
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            clients[i] = system.actorOf(Props.create(Client.class), "client" + i);
        }

        // Send start messages to the clients
        Message.WelcomeMsg startClients = new Message.WelcomeMsg(100, new ActorRef[]{checker});
        for (ActorRef client : clients) {
            client.tell(startClients, null);
        }

        // Simulate clients storing key-value pairs
        for (ActorRef client : clients) {
            for (int key = 1; key <= 100; key++) {
                client.tell(new Message.KeyValue(key, "value" + key), null);
            }
        }

        // Verify the correctness of the distributed key-value store
        Map<Integer, String> expectedData = new HashMap<>();
        for (int key = 1; key <= 100; key++) {
            expectedData.put(key, "value" + key);
        }
        checker.tell(new Message.VerifyData(expectedData), null);
    }
}
```

In this solution, the `Client` actor is responsible for storing key-value pairs and the `Checker` actor verifies the correctness of the distributed key-value store. The actors communicate using messages to exchange data and coordinate the simulation. The main method sets up the actors, sends start messages to the clients, simulates key-value storage, and verifies the correctness of the data.

